From 6d4053ed357779708e89c5f6d6952577ea652dfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri Geelen <dimitri@geelenandcompany.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:14:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] audit: the fabric drift line states coverage and which
 way the cards moved (from 832 T-525)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Fabric drift: N source file(s) have no fabric card" counts a DIFFERENCE of two quantities that
move independently: the watch set grows with the tree, registered cards grow only when someone
writes one. So "twenty files added, not carded" and "twenty cards DELETED" printed the same line.
The line now also carries the ratio and the direction, on the SAME line (T-2735's rule: one
coverage claim, never a second "registered, N unregistered" line):
  Fabric drift: U source file(s) have no fabric card — P% covered (R of W watched; NOTE)
NOTE compares registered cards with the most recent prior daily report (its "Fabric: N
registered" line): CARD LOSS (a deleted or malformed card stops participating in component
resolution), +N cards since <day>, cards flat since <day>, or "direction not evaluated" when no
prior report exists (abstain rather than print a zero delta). FABRIC_HISTORY_DIR overrides where
history is read. Cron reports are excluded. Severity is unchanged: still WARN, still only when
unregistered > 0.
Probe: tests/unit/test_t1021_fabric_coverage.py (+ _t1021_writeset_hermeticity.py). Hermetic
fixture project for the four branches, FABRIC_HISTORY_DIR per leg. Before: refuses (no coverage
line on this tree). After: 8/8.
Unchanged before and after: fabric_coverage_single_source.bats (14 ok), t3431, t3430,
fabric_watch_pattern_fitness, test_t3430_enrich_describe.py; t2298 tests 3 and 4 fail on both sides.
